\details{
The probability density function (PDF) of the Exponentiated Kumaraswamy (EKw)
distribution is given by:
\deqn{
f(x; \alpha, \beta, \lambda) = \lambda \alpha \beta x^{\alpha-1} (1 - x^\alpha)^{\beta-1} \bigl[1 - (1 - x^\alpha)^\beta \bigr]^{\lambda - 1}
